WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.740
Three temples.

2
00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:04.330
Tell them apart by looking up.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:06.490
The shared plan.

4
00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:08.470
A sanctum, called the

5
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.650
garbhagriha. A hall for

6
00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.550
worshippers, the mandapa.

7
00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:13.570
And a spire.

8
00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:16.790
NCERT names two orders, Nagara

9
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:19.207
and Dravida.

10
00:00:19.407 --> 00:00:21.187
Nagara, the north.

11
00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:23.307
The whole temple stands on a

12
00:00:23.307 --> 00:00:25.707
stone platform with steps, and

13
00:00:25.707 --> 00:00:27.487
usually has no grand boundary

14
00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:29.317
walls or gateways.

15
00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:30.730
Nagara's tower.

16
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.670
A curving shikhara, and the

17
00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:35.550
sanctum sits directly under the

18
00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:36.970
tallest one.

19
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.170
Early temples had one tower,

20
00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.880
later ones several.

21
00:00:41.373 --> 00:00:43.013
Dravida, the south.

22
00:00:43.013 --> 00:00:45.073
The temple sits inside a

23
00:00:45.073 --> 00:00:46.973
compound wall, and the front

24
00:00:46.973 --> 00:00:49.273
wall has a central gateway, the

25
00:00:49.273 --> 00:00:50.323
gopuram.

26
00:00:50.770 --> 00:00:51.810
Dravida's tower.

27
00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.830
The vimana is a stepped pyramid

28
00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:57.250
that rises geometrically.

29
00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:59.450
In the south, shikhara names

30
00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.680
only the small crown on top.

31
00:01:02.101 --> 00:01:03.221
And Vesara.

32
00:01:03.221 --> 00:01:05.821
A hybrid of the two, popular in

33
00:01:05.821 --> 00:01:07.761
the Deccan after the mid seventh

34
00:01:07.761 --> 00:01:10.121
century. Karnataka has some of

35
00:01:10.121 --> 00:01:12.251
the most experimental ones.

36
00:01:13.487 --> 00:01:14.087
For GS1:

37
00:01:14.087 --> 00:01:16.587
Nagara, Dravida and Vesara.

38
00:01:16.587 --> 00:01:19.367
Curving shikhara versus stepped

39
00:01:19.367 --> 00:01:21.867
vimana. Platform versus compound

40
00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:23.537
wall and gopuram.

41
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.550
Curve in the north.

42
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:27.350
Steps in the south.

43
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.020
Look up first.
